  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support from the Government of Australia to the Royal Thai Government&#x2019;s Vaccination Rollout against COVID-19</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to protect the health of people living in Thailand by strengthening communications for and monitoring of mass immunization campaigns against COVID-19. In collaboration with WHO, a 2-pronged approach was developed: Approach 1: Enhance data systems to improve vaccination against COVID-19, with focus on vulnerable migrant populations. Generating accurate data on numbers of individuals vaccinated is critical to monitor the progress of any vaccination campaign IOM will provide technical and financial support to local non-governmental organizations (NGOs) in four target locations, namely Songkhla, Ranong, Chiang Mai and Mae Sot, to train migrant health volunteers (MHVs) to conduct outreach vaccine information sessions and prioritization surveys in 80% of the identified at-risk migrant communities.  Approach 2: Communications for improved understanding and acceptance of COVID-19 Vaccine. Surveys will be carried out across four provinces (two targeting Myanmar migrants and two targeting Cambodian migrants), ensuring gender balance is observed.</narrative>
  </description>
